# Godot 4.6 GDScript Conventions

## General
- Use GDScript, never C#
- Use static typing everywhere: `var x: int = 0`, `func foo() -> String:`
- Use `##` for doc comments (Godot documentation comments)
- Use `#` for inline comments
- Tab indentation (Godot default)

## Autoload Singletons
- NEVER use `class_name` in Autoload scripts (causes "hides autoload singleton" error)
- Register in project.godot `[autoload]` section with `*` prefix
- Access globally: `EventBus.signal_name.emit()`, `DataManager.get_crop("carrot")`

## Signals
- Define on EventBus for cross-system communication
- Use past tense naming: `crop_planted`, `gold_changed`, `level_up`
- Always include typed parameters: `signal crop_planted(tile_pos: Vector2i, crop_id: String)`

## Data Access
- All JSON data via `DataManager.get_*()` methods
- Always return `.duplicate(true)` from query methods to ensure immutability
- Never modify data returned from DataManager directly

## Error Handling
- Use `push_error()` for fatal issues (missing files, corrupt data)
- Use `push_warning()` for recoverable issues (missing entries, fallback used)
- Never crash silently — always log

## Naming
- Files: `snake_case.gd`
- Classes: `PascalCase` (only non-Autoload scripts)
- Functions: `snake_case()`
- Private: `_prefixed`
- Constants: `UPPER_SNAKE_CASE`
- Signals: `snake_case` past tense
- Enums: `PascalCase` with `UPPER_SNAKE_CASE` values

## Testing
- Test scripts extend `Node2D`
- Place in `scenes/test/test_<system>.gd`
- Use `_assert(condition: bool, message: String)` helper
- Run with F6 (current scene only)
- Always print `=== SystemName 自动化测试 ===` header

## Pixel Art Config
- Viewport: 480x320 (30x20 tiles at 16px)
- Window: 1920x1280 (4x scale)
- Texture filter: Nearest (0)
- Stretch mode: viewport
- Stretch aspect: keep
